# Giant-squid / kraken body plan ("kraken_b") -- a long, whippy serpentine
# hunter. SHELL (K) casing SURROUNDS a MEAT (M) interior; no blubber (krakens
# do not float on fat -- the game holds them aloft as a buoyancy exception).
# Preview:  godot --headless --path . --script tools/ship_preview.gd -- ships/kraken_b.ship
#
# THE ANATOMY (owner, from the source, 2026-08-23): shell is an OUTER CASING;
# meat is INSIDE; only a LITTLE meat is EXPOSED as the deliberate WEAK SPOT.
# Reads LEFT-to-RIGHT. The LEFT end is a POINTY armoured SHELL TIP -- the mantle
# cone the squid RAMS with (shell hp 250, collision_resist 20: it barely dents).
# The armoured casing wraps the mantle top and bottom, hiding the meat interior.
# At the RIGHT the casing OPENS into the HEAD: a gaping MOUTH throat plus three
# trailing TENTACLE strands, all bare MEAT -- the exposed weak spot lives here
# (the mouth + the tentacle roots), so you snipe the head, not the shelled body.
# Buried mid-mantle is a meat-walled LOOT CAVITY -- mine through to reach it.
# One 4-connected body, no thin necks.
#
#   K shell (armour: hp 250, mass 2, collision_resist 20 -- light, very hard)
#   M meat  (dense flesh -- the mantle interior, the mouth, and the tentacles)
#   . air / hollow (the open mouth gaps and the sealed loot cavity)
#
# Composition: K 48 (30%), M 110 (70%), no W. 158 solid cells, one island.
# Shell = the mantle SKIN; meat = the bulk it encloses + the exposed head.

# MIRRORED 2026-08-24 (owner: "it is attacking with its meaty side and hurt
# itself to death"): a creature's drawn facing follows its motion with the +x
# side LEADING, so the old tip-LEFT/mouth-RIGHT authoring led with the MOUTH on
# every ram and the meat paid the bill. Flipped: the armored shell tip is now on
# the RIGHT (+x, leading -- squids jet mantle-first, tentacles trailing) and the
# exposed mouth/meat trails on the LEFT. Directional words in the prose above
# predate the flip; trust the grid.

origin 15 3

